cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Souvenance — a personal memory engine that checks each memory against its source, and the SOURCED integrity benchmark"
message: "If you use this software or refer to its architecture, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Noguera"
    given-names: "Nicolas"
    website: "https://souvenance.me"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pensine/souvenance.me"
url: "https://souvenance.me"
abstract: >-
  A self-hosted personal memory engine for AI assistants. Events are stored in
  an append-only PostgreSQL log owned by the subject; memories, embeddings and
  a bi-temporal knowledge graph are recomputable projections of that log.
  Nightly consolidation runs on a swappable AI backend, and the memory is
  served through MCP — so the model, the interface and the vendor stay
  replaceable while the substrate persists. A language model proposes each
  memory with a verbatim excerpt; code checks the excerpt against the source
  before writing, and applies the same proof gate to identity links. The
  release includes SOURCED (draft v0.1), a benchmark of write-time integrity
  on synthetic lives, with first results for three memory systems and their
  limits: one data generator written by the author, a model judge that did
  not pass its pre-registered validation, one model family throughout.
keywords:
  - personal memory
  - self-hosted
  - event sourcing
  - temporal knowledge graph
  - model context protocol
  - data ownership
  - hallucination
  - benchmark
  - verifiable AI
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
